+# Daily Grind
+
+A static homepage using native Web Components. No build step is required. Load
+`components/daily-grind.js` as a module to register the components on another page.
+
+- `<coffee-card>` accepts a heading in `slot="heading"`, descriptive content in
+  the default slot, and a native link in `slot="action"`. Choose the heading level
+  for the page context, and give repeated action links descriptive accessible names.
+- `<coffee-hero>` accepts the same slots. Keep it inside a page-level `<header>`
+  when it serves as the page banner.
+- `<grind-navigation>` accepts a brand in `slot="brand"` and native links in the
+  default slot. It owns a responsive disclosure button: Enter/Space activates the
+  native button, Escape closes the mobile menu and returns focus, and selecting
+  a link closes it. Desktop links are always visible. Listeners are removed when
+  the element disconnects and restored on reconnection.
+
+Cards and the hero delegate focus to their native links without adding extra tab
+stops. Navigation uses a native button with `aria-expanded` and a same-tree
+`aria-controls` relationship. Content stays in light DOM so it remains available
+before component registration and without JavaScript. Keep the `:not(:defined)`
+fallback rules when reusing the page layout.
+
+Styles are encapsulated in open shadow roots. Components inherit typography and
+the `--primary` and `--accent` theme properties with built-in defaults. Cards also
+support `--card-background`; the hero supports `--hero-image` (a CSS `url(...)`).
+The `card`, `hero`, `navigation`, and `toggle` parts expose larger styling hooks.
+Public custom properties can be set on any ancestor; slotted content remains
+consumer-owned.
+
+Run `npm ci` followed by `npm test` for DOM-only component checks. These checks
+cover independent instances, disclosure state, Escape/focus handling, responsive
+changes, disconnection/reconnection, and the homepage's no-script content. They
+do not replace browser or assistive-technology testing.
